%%{init: {"theme": "neutral"} }%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor M as Merchant
    participant W as mp / mobile
    participant A as Tally apps/api
    participant D as Postgres (tally)
    participant Q as Qore Catalog

    W->>A: GET /api/catalog/verticals (public, cached 10 min)
    A->>Q: GET /v1/business-taxonomy
    M->>W: shop name + sub-type (e.g. supermarket)
    W->>A: POST /api/businesses {name, subtypeCode} + Bearer JWT
    A->>A: sub-type must exist in the taxonomy → vertical
    A->>D: insert business + owner membership (one transaction)
    A-->>W: 201 business

    W->>A: GET /api/catalog/subtypes/supermarket/templates?suggestions=2
    A->>Q: GET templates (first call ~5 s, then cached)
    A-->>W: template items with suggested products + prices
    M->>W: keep / swap / add own / remove each item, set prices + opening stock

    W->>A: POST /api/businesses/:id/inventory/starter {items[] with clientRef}
    A->>A: planStarterInventory → rows + feedback (+ invalid list)
    A->>D: insert inventory_items (skip existing Qore ID or same name)<br/>+ opening stock_movements (trigger sets quantity_on_hand)
    A->>Q: POST /v1/feedback, source "template" (≤100 per call,<br/>a rejected batch is resent item by item)
    Note over A,Q: Best-effort: a catalogue failure never fails onboarding.<br/>Retrying the same request is safe (clientRef dedupe).
    A-->>W: {created, skipped, removed, invalid, feedback}
